d":true},{"surface":"டியவிற்","parts":[{"text":"டியவிற்","lemma":"டியவிற்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"கரும்புமருண்","parts":[{"text":"கரும்புமருண்","lemma":"கரும்புமருண்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"முதல","parts":[{"text":"முதல","lemma":"முதல","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பைந்தாட்","parts":[{"text":"பைந்தாட்","lemma":"பைந்தாட்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"செந்தினை","parts":[{"text":"செந்தினை","lemma":"செந்தினை","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"மட","parts":[{"text":"மட","lemma":"மட","gloss":"gentle/tender"}],"gloss":"gentle/tender","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பிடி","parts":[{"text":"பிடி","lemma":"piṭi","gloss":"female elephant"}],"gloss":"female elephant's"},{"surface":"தடக்கை","parts":[{"text":"தட","lemma":"taṭa","gloss":"large/curved"},{"text":"கை","lemma":"kai","gloss":"hand/trunk"}],"gloss":"large trunk"},{"surface":"அன்ன","parts":[{"text":"அன்ன","lemma":"anna","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like"},{"surface":"பால்","parts":[{"text":"பால்","lemma":"pāl","gloss":"milk"}],"gloss":"milk"},{"surface":"வார்பு","parts":[{"text":"வார்","lemma":"vār","gloss":"flow/pour"},{"text":"பு","lemma":"pu","gloss":"verbal participle suffix"}],"gloss":"overflowing"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கரிக்குறட்","parts":[{"text":"கரிக்குறட்","lemma":"கரிக்குறட்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"டிறைஞ்சிய","parts":[{"text":"டிறைஞ்சிய","lemma":"டிறைஞ்சிய","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"செறிகோட்","parts":[{"text":"செறிகோட்","lemma":"செறிகோட்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பைங்குரற்","parts":[{"text":"பைங்குரற்","lemma":"பைங்குரற்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"படு","parts":[{"text":"படு","lemma":"paṭu","gloss":"fall/alight"}],"gloss":"alighting"},{"surface":"கிளி","parts":[{"text":"கிளி","lemma":"kiḷi","gloss":"parrot"}],"gloss":"parrots"},{"surface":"கடிகம்","parts":[{"text":"கடி","lemma":"kaṭi","gloss":"shoo/drive away"},{"text":"கம்","lemma":"kam","gloss":"subjunctive/first-person plural suffix"}],"gloss":"we shall drive away"},{"surface":"சேறும்","parts":[{"text":"சேறும்","lemma":"சேறும்","gloss":"we will go"}],"gloss":"we will go","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அடு","parts":[{"text":"அடு","lemma":"aṭu","gloss":"kill/conquer"}],"gloss":"victorious"},{"surface":"போர்","parts":[{"text":"போர்","lemma":"pōr","gloss":"battle"}],"gloss":"battle"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"எஃகுவிளங்கு","parts":[{"text":"எஃகுவிளங்கு","lemma":"எஃகுவிளங்கு","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தடக்கை","parts":[{"text":"தடக்கை","lemma":"தடக்கை","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மலையன்","parts":[{"text":"மலையன்","lemma":"மலையன்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கானத்","parts":[{"text":"கானத்","lemma":"கானத்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"தார","parts":[{"text":"தார்","lemma":"tār","gloss":"garland"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"a","gloss":"genitive/adjectival suffix"}],"gloss":"garland's"},{"surface":"நாறும்","parts":[{"text":"நாறு","lemma":"nāṟu","gloss":"smell/fragrance"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"relative participle suffix"}],"gloss":"smelling of"},{"surface":"மார்பினை","parts":[{"text":"மார்பினை","lemma":"மார்பினை","gloss":"you who have the chest"}],"gloss":"you who have the chest","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வாரற்க","parts":[{"text":"வாரற்க","lemma":"வாரற்க","gloss":"do not come"}],"gloss":"do not come","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தில்ல","parts":[{"text":"தில்ல","lemma":"tilla","gloss":"particle of desire/emphasis"}],"gloss":"indeed"},{"surface":"வருகுவள்","parts":[{"text":"வரு","lemma":"varu","gloss":"come"},{"text":"கு","lemma":"ku","gloss":"empty morph"},{"text":"அள்","lemma":"aḷ","gloss":"she (third person feminine singular suffix)"}],"gloss":"she will come"},{"surface":"யாயே","parts":[{"text":"யாய்","lemma":"yāy","gloss":"my mother"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"my mother"}]}],"literal":"In the field where yā trees were cleared and burnt, / the red millet with green stems whose bases resemble sugarcane, / overflowing with milk like the large trunk of a gentle female elephant, / has bent down like a black anvil, with dense stalks and green ears of grain. / We shall go to drive away the alighting parrots. In the forest of Malaiyan, / who has a large hand shining with a spear of victorious battle, / O you with a chest smelling of garlands! / Do not come here, for my mother will come!","translation":"In the forest clearing where yā trees were cut and burnt, the red millet has grown with green stems whose bases resemble sugarcane. Overflowing with milk like the large trunk of a gentle female elephant, its dense stalks of green ears have bent down like black anvils. We are going there to drive away the parrots that alight on them. O lord with a chest smelling of garlands, from the forest of Malaiyan whose large hand shines with a spear of victorious battle! Do not come here, for my mother will come.","modern":"வெட்டி எரிக்கப்பட்ட யா மரங்கள் இருந்த கொல்லை நிலத்தில், கரும்பு போன்ற அடிப் பகுதியையும் பசுமையான தாளையும் உடைய செந்தினை வளர்ந்துள்ளது. மென்மையான பெண் யானையின் தும்பிக்கையைப் போலப் பால் நிறைந்து, இரும்புக் கொல்லனின் கரிக்கட்டைப் போல வளைந்த, அடர்ந்த கதிர்களைக் கொண்ட அந்தப் பசுமையான தினைப்புனத்தில் வந்து விழும் கிளிகளை ஓட்டுவதற்காக நாங்கள் அங்குச் செல்கிறோம். வெல்லும் போரில் ஏந்தும் வேல் விளங்கும் பெரிய கையை உடைய மலையனது காட்டில் உள்ள, மாலை மணம் வீசும் மார்பை உடையவனே! நீ இங்கு வரவேண்டாம்; என் தாய் அங்கு வருவாள்.","explanation":"The playmate (தோழி) is speaking to the hero (தலைவன்) who has come for a secret meeting. She tells him that the millet in the field is ripe and ready for harvest, and that they are going to the field to guard it from parrots. This belongs to the Kuriñci tiṇai (mountainous landscape), and the description of the millet field—cleared by burning yā trees, with stalks resembling sugarcane and heavy ears of grain bending like elephant trunks or black anvils—vividly depicts the fertile mountain slopes. By telling him \"do not come here, my mother will come,\" she is subtly urging him to seek a formal marriage rather than continuing secret trysts, as the period of guarding the millet field is coming to an end and the heroine will soon be confined to her home. Key words include 'செந்தினை' (red millet), 'படுகிளி கடிகம்' (we shall drive away the alighting parrots), and 'வாரற்க' (do not come).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}